From: tsf@netcom.com (Tim Freeman)
Date: Sat, 1 Oct 1994 23:23:53 -0700
Subject: [#94-10-11] Non-destructive upload? (was Re: What Happens First?)

From: hanson@hss.caltech.edu (Robin Hanson)
>Well if money were not object, you could do both - wait until you're
>really sure its just the same, *and* try out those early models -- if
>you decide you don't like who you are, turn yourself off.

The easiest way I can imagine to get the data out of a brain to
attempt an upload is to carefully disassemble it and look at how the
parts cooperate.  If, in fact, something like this comes first, then
you won't be able to try an early upload and then also try a later
upload, because attempting the former will convert your brain to
hamburger whether it succeeds or not.

Does anyone have a plausible scenario for an early upload attempt that
allows more than one try?

Tim Freeman

